{"name":"Whitewash","hex":"#fefffc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"whitewash","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mixture of a powdered mineral substance (often slaked lime (containing calcium hydroxide), chalk (calcium carbonate), or both) and water which is used for painting surfaces such as fences and walls bright white.","A thing used to hide mistakes, or to create an appearance of honesty, propriety, etc.; also , an act of hiding mistakes or creating an appearance of honesty, propriety, etc.; especially, a campaign, investigation, etc., which intentionally hides or overlooks unfavourable facts."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To paint (a building, a wall, etc.) a bright white with whitewash.","To paint (a building, a wall, etc.) a bright white with whitewash."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whitewash"}],"entries":[{"title":"Whitewash","blocks":[{"text":"Whitewash, calcimine, kalsomine, calsomine, asbestis or lime paint is a type of paint made from slaked lime (calcium hydroxide, Ca(OH)2) or chalk (calcium carbonate, CaCO3), sometimes known as \"whiting\". Various other additives are sometimes used."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Yarloop_wkshop_gnangarra_13.jpg/330px-Yarloop_wkshop_gnangarra_13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitewash","wikidata":"Q378312"},{"title":"Whitewash (sport)","blocks":[{"text":"In sport, a whitewash or sweep (N. America) is a series in which a person or team wins every game, or when a player or team wins a match to-nil."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitewash_(sport)","wikidata":"Q4019568"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Nicolae_Ionescu_-_The_Whitewashers%2C_1928.jpg/500px-Nicolae_Ionescu_-_The_Whitewashers%2C_1928.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https:/